Adds Dynamic DNS (DDNS) support for the Kea DHCP server.

Manages the kea-dhcp-ddns daemon configuration including TSIG keys,
forward and reverse DNS zones, and per-subnet DDNS policy settings
for both DHCPv4 and DHCPv6.

Integrates with the core Kea DHCP plugin via the kea_sync configure
hook to inject DDNS parameters into kea-dhcp4.conf and kea-dhcp6.conf.

Plugin Changelog
================

2.3

Added:
* Duplicate subnet validation: prevent adding multiple DDNS assignments
  for the same subnet (UniqueConstraint on DHCPv4 and DHCPv6 subnet fields).

Removed:
* Forward zone dropdown from subnet DDNS assignment dialogs. The field had
  no effect on the generated Kea configuration — the D2 daemon automatically
  matches FQDNs against all configured forward zones. The forward zones
  configuration section itself is unchanged.

2.2_1

Fixed:
* Disabled plugin no longer overwrites keactrl.conf — when core DDNS (PR #9923)
  is enabled and the plugin is disabled, the plugin's kea_sync hook was setting
  dhcp_ddns=no, preventing the kea-dhcp-ddns daemon from starting.

2.2

Added:
* Global DDNS defaults on the Settings tab: qualifying suffix, send updates,
  update on renew, replace client name, conflict resolution, and generated
  prefix. These defaults are emitted as Kea global parameters and inherited
  by all subnets unless explicitly overridden.
* Per-subnet DDNS fields now show "Use global default" as the default option.
  Only explicitly set values are emitted in the per-subnet config.

2.1_1

Fixed:
* Syslog multi-line log joining: replaced flags(syslog-protocol) with an
  explicit template() in the syslog-ng destination so that the newline rewrite
  actually takes effect. DDNS events now appear as single lines in the log
  viewer instead of 9 separate entries.

2.1

Added:
* TSIG key auto-generation: Generate button creates random secrets of the
  correct length for the selected HMAC algorithm
* Reverse zone auto-derive: dropdown in the reverse zone dialog lists all
  configured Kea subnets with their corresponding in-addr.arpa / ip6.arpa
  zone names
* DDNS status dashboard: separate Status page with daemon info (version, PID,
  uptime), global update statistics, per-TSIG-key counters, and paginated
  DDNS lease viewer showing all leases with forward/reverse DNS registrations

2.0_2

Added:
* HA sync support: register OPNsense.KeaDdns config section for XMLRPC
  sync to backup firewall via kea_ddns_xmlrpc_sync()

2.0

Changed (architectural — no core patches required):
* Replaced core patching with kea_sync configure hook. The plugin now
  post-processes kea-dhcp4.conf and kea-dhcp6.conf after core generates
  them, using the standard plugins_configure() mechanism. No OPNsense
  core files are modified.
* Survives OPNsense upgrades without reinstallation.
* Removed all patch files (26.1.patch, 26.7.patch) and generate-patch.sh.
* Simplified install/deinstall scripts — no patch application or reversal.

Fixed:
* Boot fatal on OPNsense 26.1.3 caused by removed mwexec() function.
  Plugin no longer calls any core helpers during boot or hook registration.
* Deinstall hang caused by patch prompting for input.
* All hook callbacks wrapped in try/catch to prevent system crashes.

